From d0f271de0a8efe7f74e1d89ac21cd3cf6368091c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvamalfa <salvamalfas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:46:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/19] Drop the OpenSky basic-auth fallback from the env
 template

The published API docs say OpenSky now uses OAuth2 client credentials
exclusively and that username/password no longer authenticates, so the
fallback slots were misleading. Only the client pair remains, with a note
that token refresh needs nothing else stored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYLfAv93wjCxnGdihXYpAm
---
 .env.example | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example
index eadab51..2db7e71 100644
--- a/.env.example
+++ b/.env.example
@@ -12,10 +12,9 @@ FRED_API_KEY=""
 # Optional. Seed source for the route-carrier estimator (flights per carrier per
 # route per month). Free for non-commercial use; the account has to be created
 # by hand because registration is behind a CAPTCHA.
-# Create the account at opensky-network.org, then generate an API client from
-# the account page and paste the pair here.
+# OpenSky moved to OAuth2 client credentials exclusively — username/password no
+# longer authenticates. Generate an API client from the account settings page at
+# opensky-network.org and paste the pair here. Tokens expire every 30 minutes
+# and are refreshed by the client, so nothing else needs storing.
 OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=""
 OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=""
-# Fallback if the account page offers no API client and only basic auth works.
-OPENSKY_USERNAME=""
-OPENSKY_PASSWORD=""
